{
 "_README": "Which passes-register rows price each frontier configuration at the uniform discounted tier (PI ruling D19, amended 2026-10-04: every configuration's own tokens at one tier, flex, which equals batch on the rate card). Read by scripts/lib_frontier_cost.py (FrontierCoster.configuration_cost); design in planning/wp4b-frontier-cost-design-2026-10-04.md. Each entry: 'proposer', a list of {run_id, pool, passes}, costed as passes x the pool's mean pass (all passes when 'passes' is absent); 'verifier', either {'leg': {run_id, pool}} for a full run's own verifier leg, or {'unit_from': {run_id, pool}, 'candidates': N, 'candidates_source': {file, keys}} for a rung whose union of N candidates is costed at that leg's per-call unit (one call per candidate per iteration) (the convention of scripts/stride55_ladder.py), the count copied from the committed ladder named in candidates_source. A leg that is a floor in the register (a cleanup overwrote its main record) needs 'comparables': audited legs with an identical verifier configuration, nominated here so they can be reviewed; the library refuses a nominee that is itself a floor or differs in configuration. Nominations: stride A's union leg from stride B's (same campaign, corpus and day); FOURTH's 3.7 leg from ARM2's (the 3.7 verifier on the same 55-map corpus, same campaign); TM and IM from the four complete legs of the 55-map generalisation campaign they belong to. 'units' names the unit costs the GS Pareto v2 and the K-ladder builders scale by their own formulas: 'mean_pass' is the mean pass over every listed pool; 'pooled_candidate' is the per-call unit pooled over complete legs sharing one verifier configuration. 'k_ladder_phase2_pass_units' gives each Phase 2 K-ladder family's GS pass unit (PI ruling 2026-10-04: own measured passes where recorded): 'own-gs-measured' the family's own GS passes; 't07-neighbour-mean' a T0.7 family (text or image) whose GS passes recorded no tokens, priced at the plain mean of the same family's own T0.3 and T1.0 GS passes (PI ruling 2026-10-04: every Phase 2 family rests on GS measurements; before it, the T0.7 text families used the 55-map T0.7 measurement scaled, about 7 % below their GS neighbours because the 55-map corpus is sparser). 'named' (a gs_units name) remains available but is unused. 'k_ladder_phase1_gs_stride_a' prices the gold-standard stride-A ladder's rungs: N passes of the 487-tile pool plus that rung's own verified union leg (each rung was verified separately, so no union is simulated).",
